#!ipxe
# Scout netboot menu (served by the Dell at http://192.168.1.100/boot.ipxe).
# DEFAULT IS LOCAL BOOT: the installer wipes the first internal disk, so it
# must be chosen on purpose at the machine's console.
set server 192.168.1.100
menu Scout netboot (${net0/mac})
item --gap -- Default in 15s: boot local disk
item local    Boot from local disk
item install  Install Debian trixie Scout agent box (WIPES FIRST INTERNAL DISK)
item shell    iPXE shell
choose --default local --timeout 15000 target || goto local
goto ${target}

:local
exit
exit

:install
prompt --key y --timeout 30000 Wipe first internal disk and install? Press y to continue... || goto local
kernel http://${server}/trixie/linux initrd=initrd.gz auto=true priority=critical netcfg/get_hostname=nuxci7 netcfg/get_domain=lan preseed/url=http://${server}/preseed.cfg log_host=${server} log_port=5514 video=1920x1080@60 gfxpayload=1920x1080
initrd http://${server}/trixie/initrd.gz
boot

:shell
shell
